<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Arms Warrior Pre-Raid Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Arms Warriors typically prefer running two passive trinkets. Sometimes we might use one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 5 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets, as there is no exceptional on-use trinket. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Warrior, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104993/evil-eye-of-galakras">
<img alt="Evil Eye of Galakras" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Evil Eye of Galakras</span></a>  is by far and leagues better than any other option before entering raids. This trinket is a must-obtain as it reduces the recovery rate of our talented abilities, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=46924/bladestorm">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bladestorm</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=12292/bloodbath">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bloodbath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodbath</span></a>, while also providing an immensely strong Strength proc on an internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105111/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> is generally your second-best trinket option before entering raids in Phase 5. It increases your baseline Critical Strike damage and offers a Strength Proc on an internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=104961/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> is a very powerful trinket on AoE encounters. It's special as it has a chance to proc <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146136/cleave">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cleave</span></a>, causing your attack to hit up to 5 extra targets. This trinket is going to be your second-best option on fights with 3 or more consistent targets, such as <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/1">Spoils of Pandaria </a> and <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/1">Galakras</a>.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103989/alacrity-of-xuen">
<img alt="Alacrity of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_tigergodcub.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alacrity of Xuen</span></a> is a worse alternative to the trinkets listed above, due to it not giving a preferable secondary stat. It doesn't perform better than the other in any specific scenario, but if you find yourself collecting <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=777/timeless-coin">
<span>
<img alt="Timeless Coin" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/timelesscoin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Timeless Coin</span></span></a>, it might be worth picking up.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Arms Warrior</span></h2>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak! With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons.  <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> is Arms Warriors' best alternative, offering our primary stat, Strength. Not only is the cloak 20 item-level higher than anything attainable from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6738/siege-of-orgrimmar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Siege of Orgrimmar</span></a>, but it is also the only item in the game offering more than 2 secondary stats and providing us with Hit, Crit, Haste &amp; Mastery.<br/>
<br/>This all in itself would've made the item insanely strong, but on top of that, it also has the proc <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146195/flurry-of-xuen">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_whitetiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry of Xuen</span></a>, causing you to deal AoE damage up to 5 mobs in front of you. It is to be noted that the proc can be a bit RNG, as it doesn't have an internal cooldown, but instead is RPPM (random proc per minute). From my own experience, this proc can be anywhere from 1-2% to 15% of your total damage output, depending on the encounter size and how often you can get it to proc during the encounter.<br/>
<br/>It's safe to say that your priority in Phase 5 of Mist of Pandaria Classic should be to attain your Legendary Cloak as quickly as possible.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Arms Warriors in Phase 3</span></h2>
